IO-17: make subcatchment data independent of the order of the input sections

subcatch_readSubareaParams() split the subcatchment into its three sub-areas
with Subcatch[].fracImperv, which only the [SUBCATCHMENTS] row sets; with
[SUBAREAS] above [SUBCATCHMENTS] the split used 0 % impervious and the whole
subcatchment ran as pervious. subcatch_readParams() reset the N-PERV, DSTORE
and INFIL pattern indexes, discarding [ADJUSTMENTS] rows read before it.
Keep PctZero when [SUBAREAS] is read and compute the sub-area fractions (and
the "no routing between sub-areas" rule for 0 % or 100 % impervious) in
subcatch_validate(), and initialise the pattern indexes with the other
subcatchment defaults in project.c instead of in subcatch_readParams().
Results for decks in the usual order are unchanged (same expressions);
a subcatchment without a [SUBAREAS] row keeps its all-zero sub-areas.

Requires: BND-14

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-17_swmm530.patch

